@Padraic
Chicken scratch is an old time term for handwriting that is hard to read. 
The other answer makes more sense with U.N.

@Padraic 
Grammatical point: when a noun is turned into an adjective, the singular is used. Like pencil case, 4-car garage, egg carton. These all contain more than one of the item in question, just like country house. You would never say countries house. You could conceivably say country's house, as in the house of one country, or countries' house, the house of several countries, but both are awkward. Not that awkward is off limits for a Saturday clue!

It was a good Saturday clue that tricked me for a long time.
